// src/kernel/core/drivers/dpy/table_pane.pdx -- Wave 83 G17 [G8] (#2554)
//
// GPU-accelerated tabular (grid) results-pane bind-up SKELETON for
// Wave 83 G17. A terminal shell (paideia-shell) wants to render a
// structured query result -- e.g. the output of a semantically-queried
// program trace, or a filesystem listing with heterogeneous columns --
// as a scrollable grid of (cols, rows) heterogeneous cells. Each
// column carries a width (in character cells) and an alignment knob;
// each row is a flat vector of UTF-8 cell handles. Composes with the
// Wave 78 G8 direct-scanout path (direct_scanout.pdx, #2545) and the
// Wave 79 G11 SDF atlas (sdf_atlas.pdx, #2548): the pane OWNS a GPU
// BO (via a cap handed to table_init), on table_present it STAMPS the
// grid into the BO via the atlas glyph tiles, then FLIPS the finished
// tile via direct_scanout_arm. This file is the SKELETON for the
// pane itself: a column meta table + a cell storage block + the
// ABI entrypoints the shell calls at (table_init, table_set_column,
// table_append_row, table_clear, table_present). The real body
// (glyph quad stamping, column-width justification, direct-scanout
// arm) is deferred to a follow-up slice.
//
// This file sits beside scrollback_pane.pdx (Wave 82 G15, #2552)
// which is the un-structured streaming-text sibling (append-only
// line of UTF-8 bytes vs this file's structured-record append), and
// shares the same client-of-G8+G11 posture (not a direct hardware
// driver -- a composition of the GPU BO / SDF atlas / direct-scanout
// primitives into a higher-level pane abstraction).
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 0  SCOPE + HONESTY PIN
// =============================================================================
//
// Posture: EVERY body here is a STUB per the Wave 83 G17 skeleton
// directive. The column meta layout, the cell storage layout, the
// per-pane state block, the error taxonomy, and the fingerprint
// shape are FROZEN at this skeleton stage so a follow-up slice can
// land the real body (column-width-justified rendering, SDF glyph
// quad emission into the BO, direct-scanout commit) against the
// same ABI without churn. The static state block, the fingerprint
// tags, and the counter bumps are real; no GPU memory is written
// yet, no SDF tile is stamped, no PLANE_SURF is flipped.
//
// On the Wave 83 G17 skeleton, every entrypoint:
//   (1) range-checks its inputs and refuses with the matching
//       TBL_ERR_* sentinel (0xFFFFFCB4..0xFFFFFCB8) on the first
//       failing rule;
//   (2) consults the G6 (KIND_GPU_BO_DRV, #2543) row accessors
//       (gpu_bo_row_size_pages) for the capacity gate on init;
//   (3) records the request into the single-pane state block;
//   (4) bumps the per-op counter so an operator can see the entry
//       on a boot-witness programme;
//   (5) emits a fingerprint so init / set_column / append_row /
//       clear events show up on the klog wire (present is
//       intentionally silent at skeleton stage -- the follow-up
//       slice minting the real MMIO body adds a `TABLE PRESENT
//       pipe=<dec>` line alongside the direct_scanout_arm call).
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 1  COLUMN META LAYOUT (24 bytes per column)
// =============================================================================
//
// Each column is a 24-byte record (3 u64 slots):
//
//     +0   width_chars   u64   -- column width in character cells
//                                (0 = unset; column has NOT been
//                                table_set_column'd and will render
//                                at its natural content width in the
//                                real body)
//     +8   align         u64   -- alignment knob (0=left, 1=right,
//                                2=center). Validated by the gate;
//                                values > 2 refused with
//                                TBL_ERR_BAD_ALIGN
//     +16  reserved      u64   -- reserved for the follow-up slice
//                                (fg/bg color, truncation mode,
//                                wrap flag, border style)
//
// Fixed per-table: 16 cols × 24 B = 384 B. Addressable as
// `[u64; 48]` laid out col-major: column k's three slots sit at
// `_col_meta[k*3 + 0]` .. `_col_meta[k*3 + 2]`.
//
// The column meta is written by table_set_column and read by
// table_present (follow-up). A column that was never set reports
// width=0 at render time; the follow-up renderer treats width=0 as
// "fit to content" and renders each cell at its own glyph span.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 2  CELL STORAGE LAYOUT (32 bytes per cell)
// =============================================================================
//
// Each cell is a 32-byte record (4 u64 slots):
//
//     +0   utf8_ptr    u64   -- pointer to the cell's UTF-8 bytes
//                              (0 = blank cell at skeleton stage;
//                              the real body stamps the atlas tiles
//                              for the glyph run anchored at this
//                              pointer)
//     +8   utf8_len    u64   -- byte length of the UTF-8 run
//                              (not a code-point count -- the SDF
//                              atlas lookup walks utf8_ptr for
//                              utf8_len bytes and emits one quad
//                              per decoded codepoint)
//     +16  reserved_0  u64   -- reserved for the follow-up slice
//                              (fg/bg color, attr byte, link id)
//     +24  reserved_1  u64   -- reserved for the follow-up slice
//                              (SDF-cached glyph-run quad origin
//                              offset into the GPU BO, so a
//                              re-render of an unchanged row can
//                              skip the atlas-lookup pass)
//
// Fixed per-table: 16 cols × 256 rows × 32 B = 128 KiB. Addressable
// as `[u64; 16384]` laid out row-major: cell(c, r) sits at
// `_cell_table[r*64 + c*4 + 0..3]`, where 64 = max_cols * 4 u64/cell.
//
// Row-stride discipline:
//   row_base_u64_idx = row * (16 * 4) = row << 6 (shl 6)
//   col_off_u64_idx  = col * 4        = col << 2 (shl 2)
//   cell_u64_idx     = row_base + col_off
//   cell_byte_off    = cell_u64_idx * 8 = (cell_u64_idx) << 3
//
// The skeleton does NOT write any cell slot -- table_append_row
// validates and counts but does not dereference cells_ptr. The
// follow-up slice decodes cells_ptr as an array of u64 pairs
// (utf8_ptr, utf8_len) and copies them into _cell_table at the
// head row.
//
// Size reality check -- 128 KiB in bss is ~3.5x the largest existing
// bss array in the kernel at Wave 83 landing (AHCI _ahci_cmd_table_
// pool at [u64; 4608] = 36 KiB; grep -rE '\[u64;\s*[0-9]{4,}\]' at
// landing time). The task directive's primary target was 16 cols ×
// 1024 rows = 512 KiB, with the explicit escape clause "Default to
// 256 rows if 1024 doesn't fit". Honoring that: the skeleton lands
// with TBL_MAX_ROWS = 256 (128 KiB), the follow-up slice widens to
// 1024 (512 KiB) once a kernel-link bss capacity check has run. The
// ABI gate uses the current TBL_MAX_ROWS so a caller that asks for
// rows=1024 against this landing is refused with TBL_ERR_BAD_ROWS;
// a follow-up slice retunes the constant and re-exports the same
// ABI.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 3  CELL-POINTER INPUT (cells_ptr -> array of u64 pairs)
// =============================================================================
//
// table_append_row(cells_ptr, n_cells) takes a pointer to an array
// of n_cells u64 PAIRS: cell 0 at cells_ptr[0..1], cell 1 at
// cells_ptr[2..3], etc. Each pair is (utf8_ptr, utf8_len) -- a
// handle to a run of UTF-8 bytes that the renderer stamps into the
// cell's quad.
//
// Pair stride: 16 B (2 u64). Total caller-side storage for a full
// row: 16 cells × 16 B = 256 B. The caller owns this memory for the
// duration of the call; the real body COPIES the pointer values
// into _cell_table at (head_row, c) before returning, so the caller
// may reuse the input array across appends.
//
// At skeleton stage this body:
//   (1) refuses if the pane is not inited (inited == 0 ->
//       TBL_ERR_BAD_BO);
//   (2) refuses if cells_ptr == 0 (null pointer -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO);
//   (3) refuses if n_cells == 0 or n_cells > max_cols
//       (TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS);
//   (4) refuses if cur_rows == max_rows (TBL_ERR_TABLE_FULL);
//   (5) bumps _tbl_append_ct;
//   (6) emits `TABLE APPEND row=<dec> cells=<dec>` via klog_s1_d2
//       (row = cur_rows BEFORE the bump; the follow-up slice bumps
//       cur_rows after the cell-copy loop).
//
// cur_rows is NOT advanced at skeleton stage -- the follow-up slice
// (which actually copies cells) advances it. A test witness that
// calls table_append_row at skeleton stage sees cur_rows unchanged
// and the fingerprint reports row=0 every time; the operator reads
// _tbl_append_ct for the count of attempts.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 4  CLEAR SEMANTICS (reset cur_rows + zero cell table)
// =============================================================================
//
// table_clear() resets the table to zero rows, so a follow-up
// append starts writing cells at row 0 again. The real body:
//   (1) sets _tbl_state[cur_rows_slot] = 0;
//   (2) [optional] zeros _cell_table so a reader can distinguish
//       stale rows from blank cells.
//
// The skeleton stops at step (1); _cell_table is left untouched
// because no cells were ever written. _col_meta is NOT reset by
// clear -- the column schema persists across clears so a shell can
// run the same query repeatedly without re-declaring columns.
//
// Gate: inited == 0 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 5  PRESENT SEMANTICS (direct_scanout_arm on primary pipe)
// =============================================================================
//
// table_present() flips the finished tile to the panel. Real body
// (follow-up slice):
//
//   (1) For each row r in 0..cur_rows:
//         For each col c in 0..max_cols:
//           -- decode the cell at (c, r) via its utf8_ptr/utf8_len;
//           -- justify to _col_meta[c].width_chars with _col_meta
//              [c].align;
//           -- stamp SDF glyph quads into the BO at (c, r).
//   (2) Call direct_scanout_arm(bo_cap, 0) to flip PLANE_SURF.
//
// Gate: inited == 0 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO.
//
// The skeleton stops at the gate + counter bump; it does NOT call
// direct_scanout_arm (doing so at skeleton stage would record a
// never-cleared armed state on pipe 0 in direct_scanout.pdx's per-
// pipe state block, surfacing in direct_scanout_arm_ct and
// direct_scanout_armed_bo as if the table pane had a live scanout
// -- misleading on a boot-witness programme that lands this slice
// alone). The present counter (_tbl_present_ct) is still bumped so
// the entry is visible; no fingerprint is emitted (per the Wave 83
// G17 task directive, which lists INIT / SET_COL / APPEND / CLEAR
// only).
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 6  FAILURE TAXONOMY -- 0xFFFFFCB4..0xFFFFFCB8
// =============================================================================
//
// Five codes reserved for this module. The task directive asked for
// 0xFFFFFCAF..B3; that band is CLAIMED at Wave 83 landing by
// audio_routing_channel.pdx (AUDIO_ROUTING_BAD_OP = 0xFFFFFCAF),
// hda/pin_config.pdx (HDA_PIN_CFG_BAD_INPUT = 0xFFFFFCAF), and
// pcm_ring_channel.pdx + hda/verbs.pdx + usb/hub_fsm.pdx (all three
// claim bands at 0xFFFFFCB0..0xFFFFFCBF). The sub-band
// 0xFFFFFCB4..B8 was free at landing time (`grep -rE
// '0xFFFFFCB[4-8]\b' /home/snunez/Development/PaideiaOS/` returned
// ZERO hits per slot), so this file takes 0xFFFFFCB4..B8. Values:
//
//     0xFFFFFCB4  TBL_ERR_BAD_BO       -- bo_cap == 0, or set_
//                                        column / append_row /
//                                        clear / present called on
//                                        a pane whose inited slot
//                                        is 0 (never-initialised)
//     0xFFFFFCB5  TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS     -- max_cols == 0 or max_cols
//                                        > 16 at init time; or
//                                        col_idx >= max_cols at
//                                        set_column time; or
//                                        n_cells == 0 or n_cells >
//                                        max_cols at append time
//     0xFFFFFCB6  TBL_ERR_BAD_ROWS     -- max_rows == 0, max_rows >
//                                        TBL_MAX_ROWS (256 at
//                                        skeleton), or
//                                        bo_size_bytes < max_cols *
//                                        max_rows * 32 (BO too
//                                        small to back the
//                                        requested cell count)
//     0xFFFFFCB7  TBL_ERR_BAD_ALIGN    -- align > 2 at set_column
//                                        (admitted: 0=left,
//                                        1=right, 2=center)
//     0xFFFFFCB8  TBL_ERR_TABLE_FULL   -- append_row called with
//                                        cur_rows == max_rows (no
//                                        head slot free; the shell
//                                        must call table_clear or
//                                        accept the refusal)
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 7  ENCODER POSTURE (paideia-as v0.36.82)
// =============================================================================
//
//   G1 (sized stores): the real body's cell writes use mov_q
//      (REX.W) for the per-u64 field stores (utf8_ptr / utf8_len /
//      reserved are u64 each). The static state block slots and
//      _col_meta / _cell_table are u64 so plain REX.W `mov` is
//      correct for every slot access.
//   G4 (full-register compares): every cmp here is on a 64-bit
//      register; no `cmp al, imm`, no `cmp eax, imm` short-form.
//   No `test rN, rN` -- equality-against-zero is `cmp rN, 0`.
//   No `and rN, imm64` -- the admitted path uses `and r, imm8` for
//      small masks (0x001, 0xFF) and stages larger masks via `mov
//      r10, imm64; and rN, r10` where needed. This file has no
//      large-mask operations at skeleton stage (no scroll-magnitude
//      extraction like scrollback_pane).
//   No two-operand `imul r, imm` -- the size calc (max_cols *
//      max_rows * 32) uses `imul rax, rN` (reg-reg form, admitted)
//      followed by `shl rax, 5`. Same posture as scrollback_pane
//      §E L530 (`imul rax, r13; shl rax, 4` for 16-byte cells).
//   64-bit immediates -- the return-code constants (0xFFFFFCB4..B8)
//      fit imm32 with bit 31 set, so the pdx encoder emits them via
//      the full REX.W `mov r64, imm64` form; proven form across
//      every FD/FC-band driver (direct_scanout.pdx, damage_plane.pdx,
//      scrollback_pane.pdx).
//   Multiline `pub let ="..."` is forbidden by the pdx parser;
//      every tag below is a single line.
//   Module basename matches filename basename:
//      table_pane.pdx -> module TablePane.
//   Reserved labels -- every label in this file is prefixed `tbl_`
//      so none collides with the ds_/dp_/sb_/ixc_/plpr_/kbd_/tp_
//      labels of the sibling dpy and input drivers, and none
//      accidentally spells `loop`, `if`, or `let` (paideia-as
//      reserved keywords).
//   klog wrapper discipline -- the four fingerprints each ride an
//      EXISTING wrapper to avoid gratuitous klog mint churn:
//        INIT    cols=<dec> rows=<dec>     -> klog_s1_d2
//        SET_COL col=<dec>  width=<dec>    -> klog_s1_d2
//        APPEND  row=<dec>  cells=<dec>    -> klog_s1_d2
//        CLEAR                             -> klog_s1  (0 KV)
//      klog_s1_d2 caller contract (1 stack arg = v2 at caller
//      [rsp+0]; wrapper reads at [rbp+16] after its push rbp):
//      `sub rsp, 16; mov [rsp+0], vd; CALL; add rsp, 16`. Writing
//      vd at [rsp+8] lands it at [rbp+24] inside the wrapper and
//      the real value never reaches the fingerprint -- the
//      klog_s1_d2 caller trap scrollback_pane.pdx §F called out and
//      that has burned 5+ softarchs this session.
//   Fingerprint tag length -- each [u8; N] tag's N is strlen + 1
//      (NUL terminator); tag_len off-by-one is a build-time error
//      the pdx encoder catches.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 8  STACK + REGISTER PLAN
// =============================================================================
//
// Six entrypoints (plus the cap handler):
//
//   table_init         (bo_cap, max_cols, max_rows)   -> u64
//   table_set_column   (col_idx, width_chars, align)  -> u64
//   table_append_row   (cells_ptr, n_cells)           -> u64
//   table_clear        ()                             -> u64
//   table_present      ()                             -> u64
//   cap_handler_table  (rights, target_ptr, op_arg)   -> u64
//
// All seven are non-leaf (nested calls into gpu_bo_row_size_pages /
// klog_*). Each uses the standard callee-save prologue:
//
//   push rbx; push r12; push r13;                       // 3-push, 24 B
//   -- entry rsp%16 == 8; after 3 pushes rsp%16 == 0 (pre-CALL)
//
//   push rbx; push r12; push r13; push r14; push r15;   // 5-push, 40 B
//   -- entry rsp%16 == 8; after 5 pushes rsp%16 == 0 (pre-CALL)
//
// table_init uses 5 pushes (rbx=bo_cap, r12=max_cols, r13=max_rows,
// r14=cell_bytes_need, r15=size-pages-have / state ptr). Then
// `sub rsp, 16; mov [rsp+0], r13` to stage vd=max_rows for
// klog_s1_d2 (scrollback_pane precedent, §E). `add rsp, 16`
// reclaims.
//
// table_set_column uses 3 pushes (rbx=col_idx, r12=width_chars,
// r13=align). Then `sub rsp, 16; mov [rsp+0], r12` to stage
// vd=width for klog_s1_d2. `add rsp, 16` reclaims.
//
// table_append_row uses 3 pushes (rbx=cells_ptr, r12=n_cells,
// r13=scratch for the inited gate). klog_s1_d2 takes vd=n_cells at
// caller [rsp+0]; same stack-staging discipline as set_column.
//
// table_clear uses 3 pushes (rbx/r12/r13 scratch). klog_s1 takes
// no stack arg; no stack staging needed.
//
// table_present uses 3 pushes (rbx/r12/r13 scratch). No fingerprint;
// no stack staging.
//
// cap_handler_table uses 3 pushes (rbx=rights, r12=target_ptr,
// r13=op_code). klog_s1 entry chatter needs 3 reg args only.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 9  WIRING
// =============================================================================
//
// Not wired to the smoke witness at skeleton stage. The file
// compiles alongside the kernel because tools/build.sh recurses
// through src/kernel/core/drivers/dpy/ with a single `find`, so a
// new .pdx in that directory is picked up automatically; no
// build.sh edit required.
//
// invoke.pdx gets ONE new dispatch arm (0x59 -> cap_handler_table)
// landed alongside this file (see invoke.pdx §Wave 83 G17 arm) so
// the kind is reachable from cap_invoke the moment this skeleton
// lands. 0x58 is reserved for the parallel-wave Wave 83 G16 editor
// landing; grep at landing time confirmed BOTH 0x58 and 0x59 empty
// of existing arms (`grep -nE 'cmp rcx, 0x59\b' src/kernel/core/
// cap/invoke.pdx` returned ZERO hits).
//
// No new klog wrapper is minted; the four fingerprints ride
// klog_s1_d2 (INIT, SET_COL, APPEND) and klog_s1 (CLEAR), all pre-
// existing in klog/wrappers.pdx.
//
// No caller invokes table_* yet. A follow-up slice adds a boot-
// witness programme at tests/kernel/drivers/wit_table_pane.pdx that:
//   (1) table_init(bo, 4, 16) -> TBL_OK  (small table that fits
//       in a 4-KiB Wave 75 BO: 4*16*32 = 2048 bytes, 1 page);
//   (2) table_set_column(0, 10, 0) -> TBL_OK;
//   (3) table_append_row(cells_ptr, 4) -> TBL_OK;
//   (4) table_clear() -> TBL_OK;
//   (5) table_present() -> TBL_OK;
// and asserts the INIT / SET_COL / APPEND / CLEAR fingerprints land
// on the klog wire.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 10  FOLLOW-UP SLICES
// =============================================================================
//
//   - Real cell-copy loop in table_append_row: decode cells_ptr as
//     an array of (utf8_ptr, utf8_len) pairs, store each pair into
//     _cell_table at (head_row, c), bump cur_rows.
//   - Real SDF glyph quad stamper in table_present: for each cell
//     at (c, r), look up atlas tile via sdf_atlas_lookup(codepoint)
//     for each decoded codepoint in utf8_ptr..utf8_ptr+utf8_len,
//     justify against _col_meta[c].width_chars with _col_meta[c].
//     align, copy the SDF tile into the cell's quad in the BO.
//   - Real direct_scanout_arm plumbing in table_present (behind
//     an eligibility gate on bo_cap for pipe 0).
//   - Dirty-row bitmap + damage_plane_submit integration (only
//     re-stamp the rows that changed since the last present).
//   - cap_handler extension: ops to query cur_rows / max_cols /
//     max_rows / inited (the five getters already exist as
//     entrypoints -- the handler just needs the dispatch arms);
//     the mutating ops (init / set_column / append / clear / present)
//     ride supervisor callers because their arg counts exceed the
//     cap_invoke (rights, target_ptr, op_arg) slot.
//   - gpu_bo_alloc multi-page carve so a full 16*1024 table fits
//     in a single BO; today's Wave 75 BO backs <= 128 cells
//     (4 KiB / 32 B = 128).
//   - TBL_MAX_ROWS widen from 256 to 1024 once a kernel-link bss
//     capacity check has run (the task directive's primary target
//     was 1024; the skeleton lands with 256 per the directive's
//     explicit "Default to 256 rows if 1024 doesn't fit" escape
//     clause).
// =============================================================================

module TablePane = structure {

  // ==========================================================================
  // §A  Table geometry constants
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let TBL_MAX_COLS       : u64 = 16
  pub let TBL_MAX_ROWS       : u64 = 256
  pub let TBL_CELL_BYTES     : u64 = 32
  pub let TBL_COL_META_BYTES : u64 = 24

  // Cell field offsets (within one 32-byte cell).
  pub let TBL_CELL_UTF8_PTR_OFF  : u64 = 0
  pub let TBL_CELL_UTF8_LEN_OFF  : u64 = 8
  pub let TBL_CELL_RSV0_OFF      : u64 = 16
  pub let TBL_CELL_RSV1_OFF      : u64 = 24

  // Column meta field offsets (within one 24-byte column entry).
  pub let TBL_COL_WIDTH_OFF  : u64 = 0
  pub let TBL_COL_ALIGN_OFF  : u64 = 8
  pub let TBL_COL_RSV_OFF    : u64 = 16

  // Alignment knob values (set_column admits 0..2).
  pub let TBL_ALIGN_LEFT   : u64 = 0
  pub let TBL_ALIGN_RIGHT  : u64 = 1
  pub let TBL_ALIGN_CENTER : u64 = 2

  // ==========================================================================
  // §B  Failure taxonomy -- band 0xFFFFFCB4..0xFFFFFCB8
  //
  // See §6 of the file header for the band provenance (task directive
  // asked for 0xFFFFFCAF..B3; that band is claimed by audio_routing_
  // channel, hda/pin_config, pcm_ring_channel, hda/verbs, usb/hub_fsm,
  // so this file takes a free quintet at 0xFFFFFCB4..B8).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let TBL_OK                : u64 = 0
  pub let TBL_ERR_BAD_BO        : u64 = 0xFFFFFCB4
  pub let TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS      : u64 = 0xFFFFFCB5
  pub let TBL_ERR_BAD_ROWS      : u64 = 0xFFFFFCB6
  pub let TBL_ERR_BAD_ALIGN     : u64 = 0xFFFFFCB7
  pub let TBL_ERR_TABLE_FULL    : u64 = 0xFFFFFCB8

  // ==========================================================================
  // §C  Pane state -- 5 u64 slots for the single global table.
  //
  // Layout (40 bytes total):
  //   +0   bo_cap          -- GPU BO cap backing the render output
  //                           (0 before init; non-zero after)
  //   +8   max_cols        -- columns admitted at init time
  //   +16  max_rows        -- rows admitted at init time
  //   +24  cur_rows        -- rows currently populated (0..max_rows)
  //   +32  inited          -- 1 iff table_init succeeded
  //
  // Single table per shell at Wave 83 (same posture as scrollback_
  // pane). A follow-up slice promotes this to a slab (one row per
  // table cap) once multi-table shells land.
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let mut _tbl_state : [u64; 5] = uninit @align(64)

  // Per-op stats (bumped once per successful entry). Visible via
  // the getter sextet in §K.
  pub let mut _tbl_init_ct    : u64 = 0
  pub let mut _tbl_scol_ct    : u64 = 0
  pub let mut _tbl_append_ct  : u64 = 0
  pub let mut _tbl_clear_ct   : u64 = 0
  pub let mut _tbl_present_ct : u64 = 0

  // ==========================================================================
  // §D  Column meta table -- 16 cols × 24 B = 384 B
  //
  // Row-major as described in §1. col k's slots:
  //     _col_meta[k*3 + 0]  = width_chars
  //     _col_meta[k*3 + 1]  = align
  //     _col_meta[k*3 + 2]  = reserved
  //
  // Zero-initialised by .bss; a column that was never set reports
  // width=0 (natural width) and align=0 (left).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let mut _col_meta : [u64; 48] = uninit @align(64)

  // ==========================================================================
  // §E  Cell storage table -- 16 cols × 256 rows × 32 B = 128 KiB
  //
  // Row-major as described in §2. cell(c, r) at:
  //     _cell_table[r * 64 + c * 4 + 0] = utf8_ptr
  //     _cell_table[r * 64 + c * 4 + 1] = utf8_len
  //     _cell_table[r * 64 + c * 4 + 2] = reserved_0
  //     _cell_table[r * 64 + c * 4 + 3] = reserved_1
  //
  // Zero-initialised by .bss. @align(4096) so the follow-up slice
  // can map this into the GPU BO's host-visible view in a single
  // page-aligned window.
  //
  // Skeleton does NOT touch this table; present time is the only
  // reader and present is deferred.
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let mut _cell_table : [u64; 16384] = uninit @align(4096)

  // ==========================================================================
  // §F  Fingerprint tags + keys
  //
  // Four tags, one per observable entrypoint (present is silent at
  // skeleton stage per the Wave 83 G17 task directive). Each is a
  // single-line string literal (the multiline `pub let ="..."` form
  // is forbidden by the pdx parser). Tag length is `strlen + 1`
  // (NUL terminator) so a tag_len off-by-one is a build-time error.
  //
  // Fingerprints on the wire:
  //   TABLE INIT cols=<dec> rows=<dec>
  //   TABLE SET_COL col=<dec> width=<dec>
  //   TABLE APPEND row=<dec> cells=<dec>
  //   TABLE CLEAR
  //
  // Matches tests/fingerprints/table_pane.golden pattern.
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let tbl_tag_init    : [u8; 11] = "TABLE INIT\0"
  pub let tbl_tag_set_col : [u8; 14] = "TABLE SET_COL\0"
  pub let tbl_tag_append  : [u8; 13] = "TABLE APPEND\0"
  pub let tbl_tag_clear   : [u8; 12] = "TABLE CLEAR\0"

  pub let tbl_k_cols  : [u8; 5] = "cols\0"
  pub let tbl_k_rows  : [u8; 5] = "rows\0"
  pub let tbl_k_col   : [u8; 4] = "col\0"
  pub let tbl_k_width : [u8; 6] = "width\0"
  pub let tbl_k_row   : [u8; 4] = "row\0"
  pub let tbl_k_cells : [u8; 6] = "cells\0"

  // Handler-entry chatter tag (for the cap-handler path).
  pub let tbl_tag_handler_entry : [u8; 20] = "TABLE handler entry\0"

  // ==========================================================================
  // §G  table_init(bo_cap, max_cols, max_rows) -> u64
  //
  // Initialise the global table pane: validate (max_cols, max_rows)
  // against the fixed limits, validate bo_cap is nonzero AND its
  // backing memory is large enough for (max_cols * max_rows * 32)
  // bytes, then record the geometry + bo_cap + reset cur_rows.
  //
  // Gates in order:
  //   (R1) max_cols == 0 || max_cols > TBL_MAX_COLS -> TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS
  //   (R2) max_rows == 0 || max_rows > TBL_MAX_ROWS -> TBL_ERR_BAD_ROWS
  //   (R3) bo_cap == 0                              -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO
  //   (R4) gpu_bo_row_size_pages(bo_cap) * 4096 <
  //        max_cols * max_rows * 32                 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_ROWS
  //
  // On admission the body:
  //   (a) writes bo_cap   to _tbl_state[0];
  //   (b) writes max_cols to _tbl_state[8];
  //   (c) writes max_rows to _tbl_state[16];
  //   (d) writes 0        to _tbl_state[24] (cur_rows);
  //   (e) writes 1        to _tbl_state[32] (inited);
  //   (f) bumps _tbl_init_ct;
  //   (g) emits `TABLE INIT cols=<dec> rows=<dec>` via klog_s1_d2.
  //
  // No fingerprint on the gate-failing paths -- the error code in
  // rax is the only observable, same posture as scrollback_pane and
  // direct_scanout. Re-init (calling init twice) is admitted and
  // overwrites the state -- the second init validates against the
  // second BO's size as the first did; a follow-up slice may add a
  // reinit-is-refused gate if the shell relies on the first init
  // being terminal.
  //
  // SysV: rdi = bo_cap, rsi = max_cols, rdx = max_rows.
  // Stack recipe: 5 callee-save pushes (rbx = bo_cap, r12 = max_cols,
  //   r13 = max_rows, r14 = cell_bytes_need, r15 = state base ptr).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let table_init : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{boot} =
    fn (bo_cap: u64, max_cols: u64, max_rows: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {boot},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: validation gate chain over (bo_cap, max_cols, max_rows). Rules in order: (R1) max_cols == 0 || max_cols > TBL_MAX_COLS(16) -> TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS (0xFFFFFCB5); (R2) max_rows == 0 || max_rows > TBL_MAX_ROWS(256 at skeleton; task directive's primary 1024 target deferred to follow-up via the explicit `Default to 256 rows if 1024 doesn't fit` escape clause) -> TBL_ERR_BAD_ROWS (0xFFFFFCB6); (R3) bo_cap == 0 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO (0xFFFFFCB4); (R4) gpu_bo_row_size_pages(bo_cap) * 4096 < max_cols * max_rows * 32 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_ROWS (BO too small; same error class as R2 because the resolution is the same -- the caller reduces rows). Admission records (bo_cap, max_cols, max_rows, 0, 1) at _tbl_state + bumps _tbl_init_ct + emits `TABLE INIT cols=<dec> rows=<dec>` via klog_s1_d2 (v2=max_rows at caller [rsp+0]). Register plan: rbx = bo_cap (saved), r12 = max_cols (saved), r13 = max_rows (saved), r14 = cell-bytes-need scratch, r15 = have-bytes / _tbl_state base pointer. Five callee-save pushes land rsp%16==0 at every nested call (entry %16==8, +40 -> 48, %16==0). klog_s1_d2 caller contract: `sub rsp, 16; mov [rsp+0], r13` writes v2=max_rows to caller [rsp+0] -- which the wrapper reads at [rbp+16] after its own `push rbp`. Writing v2 at [rsp+8] would land it at [rbp+24] inside the wrapper and the real max_rows value never reaches the fingerprint (the klog_s1_d2 caller trap scrollback_pane.pdx §F called out). `add rsp, 16` reclaims pad + v2 slot. Size calc: `imul rax, r13; shl rax, 5` is (max_cols * max_rows) * 32 (admitted 2-op `imul reg,reg`; the pdx encoder forbids 2-op `imul r, imm` but admits reg-reg; see scrollback_pane.pdx §E L530 precedent). Labels prefixed tbl_init_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;
        push r14;
        push r15;

        mov rbx, rdi;                       // rbx = bo_cap (saved)
        mov r12, rsi;                       // r12 = max_cols (saved)
        mov r13, rdx;                       // r13 = max_rows (saved)

        // --- Gate (R1): max_cols in (0, TBL_MAX_COLS].
        cmp r12, 0;
        je  tbl_init_bad_cols;
        mov r10, 16;                        // TBL_MAX_COLS
        cmp r12, r10;
        ja  tbl_init_bad_cols;

        // --- Gate (R2): max_rows in (0, TBL_MAX_ROWS].
        cmp r13, 0;
        je  tbl_init_bad_rows;
        mov r10, 256;                       // TBL_MAX_ROWS (skeleton)
        cmp r13, r10;
        ja  tbl_init_bad_rows;

        // --- Gate (R3): bo_cap != 0.
        cmp rbx, 0;
        je  tbl_init_bad_bo;

        // --- Gate (R4): size check.
        //     need_bytes = max_cols * max_rows * 32.
        //     have_bytes = size_pages * 4096 = size_pages << 12.
        //     if have_bytes < need_bytes -> TBL_ERR_BAD_ROWS.
        mov rdi, rbx;
        call gpu_bo_row_size_pages;
        // rax = size_pages (or GPU_BO_DECODE_BAD = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF).
        // On DECODE_BAD, shl rax, 12 saturates high and the size-
        // compare below treats the row as "large enough" by false-
        // positive; the real-body slice intercepts DECODE_BAD
        // explicitly. At skeleton stage, DECODE_BAD on R3-passing
        // (bo_cap != 0) implies a bogus cap, and the admission is
        // harmless because no cell is written.
        shl rax, 12;                        // rax = have_bytes
        mov r15, rax;                       // r15 = have_bytes (temp)

        //     need_bytes = (max_cols * max_rows) * 32.
        mov rax, r12;                       // rax = max_cols
        imul rax, r13;                      // rax = max_cols * max_rows
        shl rax, 5;                         // rax = * 32
        mov r14, rax;                       // r14 = need_bytes

        cmp r15, r14;                       // have vs need
        jb  tbl_init_bad_rows;

        // --- Admitted. Compute _tbl_state base.
        lea r15, [rip + _tbl_state];

        // --- Record state.
        mov [r15 + 0],  rbx;                // bo_cap
        mov [r15 + 8],  r12;                // max_cols
        mov [r15 + 16], r13;                // max_rows
        xor rax, rax;
        mov [r15 + 24], rax;                // cur_rows = 0
        mov rax, 1;
        mov [r15 + 32], rax;                // inited = 1

        // --- Count the init (bump BEFORE fingerprint so a crash
        //     mid-fingerprint still records the entry).
        mov rax, [rip + _tbl_init_ct];
        add rax, 1;
        mov [rip + _tbl_init_ct], rax;

        // --- klog_s1_d2(level=3, SUBSYS_DRV_, tag_init, k_cols,
        //                max_cols, k_rows, [v2=max_rows]).
        //
        // After 5 callee-save pushes rsp%16==0 (entry %16==8, +40 =
        // 48, %16==0). `sub rsp, 16` reserves the v2 slot AND keeps
        // alignment; the wrapper reads v2 at [rbp+16] after its own
        // `push rbp` (which is exactly what caller [rsp+0] + CALL
        // (-8) + push rbp (-8) resolves to).
        sub rsp, 16;
        mov [rsp + 0], r13;                 // v2 = max_rows (caller [rsp+0])
        mov rdi, 3;                         // LEVEL_INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_DRV_];
        lea rdx, [rip + tbl_tag_init];
        lea rcx, [rip + tbl_k_cols];
        mov r8, r12;                        // v1 = max_cols
        lea r9, [rip + tbl_k_rows];
        call klog_s1_d2;
        add rsp, 16;                        // reclaim pad + v2 slot

        xor rax, rax;                       // TBL_OK
        jmp tbl_init_out;

      tbl_init_bad_cols:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCB5;                // TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS
        jmp tbl_init_out;
      tbl_init_bad_rows:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCB6;                // TBL_ERR_BAD_ROWS
        jmp tbl_init_out;
      tbl_init_bad_bo:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCB4;                // TBL_ERR_BAD_BO

      tbl_init_out:
        pop r15;
        pop r14;
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §H  table_set_column(col_idx, width_chars, align) -> u64
  //
  // Set the (width, align) meta for one column. The real body writes
  // _col_meta[col_idx*3 + 0] = width and _col_meta[col_idx*3 + 1] =
  // align; the skeleton does the write unconditionally once the gates
  // pass (the write is static-safe -- no pointer deref beyond the
  // bss-resident _col_meta array).
  //
  // Gates in order:
  //   (R1) inited == 0                       -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO
  //   (R2) col_idx >= max_cols               -> TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS
  //   (R3) align > TBL_ALIGN_CENTER (= 2)    -> TBL_ERR_BAD_ALIGN
  //
  // Admission:
  //   (a) write width_chars to _col_meta[col_idx*3 + 0];
  //   (b) write align       to _col_meta[col_idx*3 + 1];
  //   (c) bump _tbl_scol_ct;
  //   (d) emit `TABLE SET_COL col=<dec> width=<dec>` via klog_s1_d2.
  //
  // SysV: rdi = col_idx, rsi = width_chars, rdx = align.
  // Stack recipe: 3 callee-save pushes (rbx = col_idx, r12 = width,
  //   r13 = align).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let table_set_column : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{boot} =
    fn (col_idx: u64, width_chars: u64, align: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {boot},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: refuses if _tbl_state[32] (inited) == 0 (TBL_ERR_BAD_BO 0xFFFFFCB4), if col_idx >= _tbl_state[8] (max_cols) (TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS 0xFFFFFCB5), or if align > 2 (TBL_ERR_BAD_ALIGN 0xFFFFFCB7; admitted 0=left, 1=right, 2=center). On admission writes width_chars to _col_meta[col_idx*3+0], align to _col_meta[col_idx*3+1], bumps _tbl_scol_ct, and emits `TABLE SET_COL col=<dec> width=<dec>` via klog_s1_d2 (v2=width_chars at caller [rsp+0]). Column index -> _col_meta u64 index: col_idx * 3 computed as (col_idx<<1)+col_idx, which in reg form is `mov r10, rbx; shl r10, 1; add r10, rbx` (2*k + k = 3*k; avoids 2-op `imul r, imm` which the pdx encoder forbids). Column byte offset: (col_idx*3) << 3 = col_idx * 24, so `shl r10, 3` on the index converts to byte offset. Register plan: rbx = col_idx (saved), r12 = width_chars (saved), r13 = align (saved). Three callee-save pushes land rsp%16==0 at every nested call (entry %16==8, +24 = 32, %16==0). klog_s1_d2 caller contract: `sub rsp, 16; mov [rsp+0], r12` writes v2=width_chars to caller [rsp+0]. Labels prefixed tbl_scol_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;

        mov rbx, rdi;                       // rbx = col_idx (saved)
        mov r12, rsi;                       // r12 = width_chars (saved)
        mov r13, rdx;                       // r13 = align (saved)

        // --- Gate (R1): inited == 0 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO.
        lea r10, [rip + _tbl_state];
        mov r11, [r10 + 32];                // r11 = inited
        cmp r11, 0;
        je  tbl_scol_bad_bo;

        // --- Gate (R2): col_idx >= max_cols -> TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS.
        mov r11, [r10 + 8];                 // r11 = max_cols
        cmp rbx, r11;
        jae tbl_scol_bad_cols;

        // --- Gate (R3): align > 2 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_ALIGN.
        mov r11, 2;                         // TBL_ALIGN_CENTER
        cmp r13, r11;
        ja  tbl_scol_bad_align;

        // --- Compute _col_meta byte offset:
        //     col_u64_idx  = col_idx * 3
        //     col_byte_off = col_u64_idx * 8 = col_idx * 24
        //     (3-element stride; 2-op `imul r, imm` forbidden, so
        //      compute as 2k + k via a shift-add.)
        mov r10, rbx;                       // r10 = col_idx
        shl r10, 1;                         // r10 = col_idx * 2
        add r10, rbx;                       // r10 = col_idx * 3
        shl r10, 3;                         // r10 = col_idx * 24 (byte off)

        // --- Base pointer to _col_meta.
        lea r11, [rip + _col_meta];
        add r11, r10;                       // r11 = &_col_meta[col_idx]

        // --- Store width + align (reserved slot untouched -- bss zero).
        mov [r11 + 0], r12;                 // width_chars
        mov [r11 + 8], r13;                 // align

        // --- Count the set_column.
        mov rax, [rip + _tbl_scol_ct];
        add rax, 1;
        mov [rip + _tbl_scol_ct], rax;

        // --- klog_s1_d2(level=3, SUBSYS_DRV_, tag_set_col, k_col,
        //                col_idx, k_width, [v2=width_chars]).
        sub rsp, 16;
        mov [rsp + 0], r12;                 // v2 = width_chars (caller [rsp+0])
        mov rdi, 3;                         // LEVEL_INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_DRV_];
        lea rdx, [rip + tbl_tag_set_col];
        lea rcx, [rip + tbl_k_col];
        mov r8, rbx;                        // v1 = col_idx
        lea r9, [rip + tbl_k_width];
        call klog_s1_d2;
        add rsp, 16;                        // reclaim pad + v2 slot

        xor rax, rax;                       // TBL_OK
        jmp tbl_scol_out;

      tbl_scol_bad_bo:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCB4;                // TBL_ERR_BAD_BO
        jmp tbl_scol_out;
      tbl_scol_bad_cols:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCB5;                // TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS
        jmp tbl_scol_out;
      tbl_scol_bad_align:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCB7;                // TBL_ERR_BAD_ALIGN

      tbl_scol_out:
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §I  table_append_row(cells_ptr, n_cells) -> u64
  //
  // Append one row of n_cells cell handles. Each handle is a 16-byte
  // (utf8_ptr, utf8_len) pair in a flat array at cells_ptr. The real
  // body copies each pair into _cell_table at (cur_rows, c) and
  // bumps cur_rows; the skeleton validates, bumps the counter, and
  // emits the fingerprint without touching _cell_table.
  //
  // Gates in order:
  //   (R1) inited == 0                       -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO
  //   (R2) cells_ptr == 0                    -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO
  //   (R3) n_cells == 0 || n_cells > max_cols -> TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS
  //   (R4) cur_rows == max_rows              -> TBL_ERR_TABLE_FULL
  //
  // On admission the body:
  //   (a) bumps _tbl_append_ct;
  //   (b) emits `TABLE APPEND row=<dec> cells=<dec>` via klog_s1_d2
  //       (row = cur_rows BEFORE the follow-up slice bumps it).
  //
  // The skeleton does NOT bump cur_rows (that advances on real cell
  // copy, which happens in the follow-up); a witness that calls
  // append_row at skeleton stage sees cur_rows=0 forever and reads
  // _tbl_append_ct for the attempt count.
  //
  // SysV: rdi = cells_ptr, rsi = n_cells.
  // Stack recipe: 3 callee-save pushes (rbx = cells_ptr, r12 =
  //   n_cells, r13 = scratch for state slot reads).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let table_append_row : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{boot} =
    fn (cells_ptr: u64, n_cells: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {boot},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: refuses if _tbl_state[32] (inited) == 0 (TBL_ERR_BAD_BO 0xFFFFFCB4), if cells_ptr == 0 (also TBL_ERR_BAD_BO, treating a null handle array as a bad input), if n_cells == 0 or n_cells > _tbl_state[8] (max_cols) (TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS 0xFFFFFCB5), or if _tbl_state[24] (cur_rows) == _tbl_state[16] (max_rows) (TBL_ERR_TABLE_FULL 0xFFFFFCB8). On admission bumps _tbl_append_ct + emits `TABLE APPEND row=<dec> cells=<dec>` via klog_s1_d2 (row=cur_rows BEFORE any bump; the real body in the follow-up slice copies cells into _cell_table then bumps cur_rows). The row=0 reported by the skeleton forever is INTENTIONAL at skeleton stage -- no cells are written yet -- and the klog operator reads _tbl_append_ct for the attempt count. UTF-8 decode + cell stamping are deferred to the follow-up slice. Register plan: rbx = cells_ptr (saved), r12 = n_cells (saved), r13 = scratch for state slot reads + row-for-fingerprint. Three callee-save pushes land rsp%16==0 at every nested call. klog_s1_d2 caller contract: `sub rsp, 16; mov [rsp+0], r12` writes v2=n_cells to caller [rsp+0]. Labels prefixed tbl_app_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;

        mov rbx, rdi;                       // rbx = cells_ptr (saved)
        mov r12, rsi;                       // r12 = n_cells (saved)

        // --- Gate (R1): inited == 0 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO.
        lea r10, [rip + _tbl_state];
        mov r11, [r10 + 32];                // r11 = inited
        cmp r11, 0;
        je  tbl_app_bad_bo;

        // --- Gate (R2): cells_ptr == 0 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO.
        cmp rbx, 0;
        je  tbl_app_bad_bo;

        // --- Gate (R3): n_cells in (0, max_cols].
        cmp r12, 0;
        je  tbl_app_bad_cols;
        mov r11, [r10 + 8];                 // r11 = max_cols
        cmp r12, r11;
        ja  tbl_app_bad_cols;

        // --- Gate (R4): cur_rows < max_rows -> else TBL_ERR_TABLE_FULL.
        mov r13, [r10 + 24];                // r13 = cur_rows (BEFORE bump)
        mov r11, [r10 + 16];                // r11 = max_rows
        cmp r13, r11;
        jae tbl_app_full;

        // --- cell copy DEFERRED to the follow-up slice. Skeleton
        //     proceeds to counter bump + fingerprint without
        //     touching _cell_table or _tbl_state[24].

        // --- Count the append.
        mov rax, [rip + _tbl_append_ct];
        add rax, 1;
        mov [rip + _tbl_append_ct], rax;

        // --- klog_s1_d2(level=3, SUBSYS_DRV_, tag_append, k_row,
        //                r13 /*cur_rows*/, k_cells, [v2=n_cells]).
        sub rsp, 16;
        mov [rsp + 0], r12;                 // v2 = n_cells (caller [rsp+0])
        mov rdi, 3;                         // LEVEL_INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_DRV_];
        lea rdx, [rip + tbl_tag_append];
        lea rcx, [rip + tbl_k_row];
        mov r8, r13;                        // v1 = cur_rows (row)
        lea r9, [rip + tbl_k_cells];
        call klog_s1_d2;
        add rsp, 16;                        // reclaim pad + v2 slot

        xor rax, rax;                       // TBL_OK
        jmp tbl_app_out;

      tbl_app_bad_bo:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCB4;                // TBL_ERR_BAD_BO
        jmp tbl_app_out;
      tbl_app_bad_cols:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCB5;                // TBL_ERR_BAD_COLS
        jmp tbl_app_out;
      tbl_app_full:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCB8;                // TBL_ERR_TABLE_FULL

      tbl_app_out:
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §J  table_clear() -> u64
  //
  // Reset cur_rows to 0 so a follow-up append writes at row 0 again.
  // The column schema (_col_meta) is NOT reset -- the shell may run
  // the same query repeatedly without re-declaring columns.
  //
  // Gate (R1): inited == 0 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO.
  //
  // On admission the body:
  //   (a) writes 0 to _tbl_state[24] (cur_rows);
  //   (b) bumps _tbl_clear_ct;
  //   (c) emits `TABLE CLEAR` via klog_s1 (0 KV entries).
  //
  // _cell_table is NOT zeroed at skeleton stage because no cells
  // have been written; a follow-up slice may add a defensive zero
  // once the cell-copy body lands and dirty cells can accumulate
  // across appends.
  //
  // SysV: no args.
  // Stack recipe: 3 callee-save pushes (rbx/r12/r13 scratch).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let table_clear : () -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{boot} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {boot},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: refuses if _tbl_state[32] (inited) == 0 (TBL_ERR_BAD_BO 0xFFFFFCB4). On admission zeros _tbl_state[24] (cur_rows), bumps _tbl_clear_ct, and emits `TABLE CLEAR` via klog_s1 (0 KV; the tag alone carries the signal -- there is no interesting payload to log at clear time). _col_meta is INTENTIONALLY not reset -- the column schema persists across clears so a shell can run the same query repeatedly without re-declaring columns. _cell_table is left untouched because no cells were ever written at skeleton stage; the follow-up slice may add a defensive zero pass once the cell-copy body lands. Register plan: rbx = scratch for state base. Three callee-save pushes land rsp%16==0 (entry %16==8, +24 = 32, %16==0). klog_s1 takes rdi=level, rsi=subsys, rdx=tag -- all three regs, no stack staging. Labels prefixed tbl_clr_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;

        // --- Gate (R1): inited == 0 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO.
        lea rbx, [rip + _tbl_state];
        mov r10, [rbx + 32];                // r10 = inited
        cmp r10, 0;
        je  tbl_clr_bad_bo;

        // --- Reset cur_rows to 0.
        xor rax, rax;
        mov [rbx + 24], rax;                // cur_rows = 0

        // --- Count the clear.
        mov rax, [rip + _tbl_clear_ct];
        add rax, 1;
        mov [rip + _tbl_clear_ct], rax;

        // --- klog_s1(level=3, SUBSYS_DRV_, tag_clear). 0 KV; no
        //     stack staging; all three args in rdi/rsi/rdx.
        mov rdi, 3;                         // LEVEL_INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_DRV_];
        lea rdx, [rip + tbl_tag_clear];
        call klog_s1;

        xor rax, rax;                       // TBL_OK
        jmp tbl_clr_out;

      tbl_clr_bad_bo:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCB4;                // TBL_ERR_BAD_BO

      tbl_clr_out:
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §K  table_present() -> u64
  //
  // Flip the finished table tile to the panel via the Wave 78 G8
  // direct-scanout path. Real body (follow-up slice):
  //
  //   (1) For each row r in 0..cur_rows:
  //         For each col c in 0..max_cols:
  //           decode (utf8_ptr, utf8_len) at _cell_table[r*64 + c*4..];
  //           justify to _col_meta[c].width_chars with _col_meta[c].align;
  //           stamp SDF glyph quads into the BO at (c, r).
  //   (2) Call direct_scanout_eligibility(bo_cap, 0, w, h) -> if not
  //       DS_OK return the sentinel verbatim.
  //   (3) Call direct_scanout_arm(bo_cap, 0) to flip PLANE_SURF.
  //
  // Gate (R1): inited == 0 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO.
  //
  // At skeleton stage the body gate-checks and bumps _tbl_present_ct
  // only. It does NOT call direct_scanout_arm because doing so would
  // record a never-cleared armed state on pipe 0 in direct_scanout's
  // per-pipe state block, polluting direct_scanout_arm_ct and
  // direct_scanout_armed_bo for any boot-witness programme that
  // lands this slice alone. No fingerprint is emitted (per the Wave
  // 83 G17 task directive, which lists INIT / SET_COL / APPEND /
  // CLEAR only).
  //
  // SysV: no args.
  // Stack recipe: 3 callee-save pushes (rbx/r12/r13 scratch).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let table_present : () -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{boot} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {boot},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: refuses if _tbl_state[32] (inited) == 0 (TBL_ERR_BAD_BO 0xFFFFFCB4). On admission bumps _tbl_present_ct and returns TBL_OK. The real body (follow-up) walks (cur_rows x max_cols) cells, stamps SDF glyph quads into the BO via sdf_atlas_lookup, then calls direct_scanout_eligibility + direct_scanout_arm; the skeleton omits those calls because arming the pipe would surface in direct_scanout_arm_ct / direct_scanout_armed_bo on a boot-witness programme as if the table had a live scanout -- misleading when no scanout work has happened. No fingerprint per the Wave 83 G17 task directive (INIT / SET_COL / APPEND / CLEAR only). Register plan: rbx = scratch for state slot. Three callee-save pushes land rsp%16==0 (entry %16==8, +24 = 32, %16==0) in case the follow-up slice adds nested calls (direct_scanout_arm) without reshaping the prologue. Labels prefixed tbl_pres_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;

        // --- Gate (R1): inited == 0 -> TBL_ERR_BAD_BO.
        lea rbx, [rip + _tbl_state];
        mov r10, [rbx + 32];                // r10 = inited
        cmp r10, 0;
        je  tbl_pres_bad_bo;

        // --- direct_scanout_arm call DEFERRED (see justification).
        //     Skeleton bumps the counter and returns TBL_OK.

        mov rax, [rip + _tbl_present_ct];
        add rax, 1;
        mov [rip + _tbl_present_ct], rax;

        xor rax, rax;                       // TBL_OK
        jmp tbl_pres_out;

      tbl_pres_bad_bo:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCB4;                // TBL_ERR_BAD_BO

      tbl_pres_out:
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §L  Table-state getters
  //
  // Leaf getters so a boot-witness programme can assert the table's
  // state without touching the _tbl_state symbol directly.
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let table_inited : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: single mov load from _tbl_state[32] (inited). Leaf.",
      block: {
        lea rax, [rip + _tbl_state];
        mov rax, [rax + 32];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let table_cols : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: single mov load from _tbl_state[8] (max_cols). Leaf.",
      block: {
        lea rax, [rip + _tbl_state];
        mov rax, [rax + 8];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let table_rows : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: single mov load from _tbl_state[16] (max_rows). Leaf.",
      block: {
        lea rax, [rip + _tbl_state];
        mov rax, [rax + 16];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let table_cur_rows : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: single mov load from _tbl_state[24] (cur_rows). Leaf.",
      block: {
        lea rax, [rip + _tbl_state];
        mov rax, [rax + 24];
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §M  Per-op counter getters
  //
  // Five leaf getters so a boot-witness programme can assert the
  // (init_ct, scol_ct, append_ct, clear_ct, present_ct) tuple
  // without touching the _tbl_*_ct symbols directly.
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let table_init_ct : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: single mov load from _tbl_init_ct. Leaf.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rip + _tbl_init_ct];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let table_scol_ct : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: single mov load from _tbl_scol_ct. Leaf.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rip + _tbl_scol_ct];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let table_append_ct : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: single mov load from _tbl_append_ct. Leaf.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rip + _tbl_append_ct];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let table_clear_ct : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: single mov load from _tbl_clear_ct. Leaf.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rip + _tbl_clear_ct];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let table_present_ct : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: single mov load from _tbl_present_ct. Leaf.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rip + _tbl_present_ct];
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §N  cap_handler_table(rights, target_ptr, op_arg) -> u64
  //
  // KIND_TABLE_PANE (0x59) cap_invoke dispatch handler. Reachable
  // from cap/invoke.pdx:cap_invoke_dispatch via the `cmp rcx, 0x59;
  // je call_kind_table_pane` arm added alongside this file.
  //
  // The five main entrypoints each take more arguments than cap_
  // invoke's (rights, target_ptr, op_arg) slot admits (init takes 3,
  // set_column takes 3, append takes 2 including a pointer, clear
  // takes 0, present takes 0). clear / present ALONE fit -- but at
  // skeleton stage even those are query-only here because arming
  // the scanout would pollute the sibling driver's state block (see
  // §K). The handler is therefore QUERY-ONLY at skeleton stage,
  // exactly like direct_scanout / damage_plane / sdf_atlas /
  // scrollback_pane do for their first slice. Six ops:
  //
  //     op 0 TBL_OP_QUERY_INITED      -> _tbl_state[32] (inited)
  //     op 1 TBL_OP_QUERY_INIT_CT     -> _tbl_init_ct
  //     op 2 TBL_OP_QUERY_SCOL_CT     -> _tbl_scol_ct
  //     op 3 TBL_OP_QUERY_APPEND_CT   -> _tbl_append_ct
  //     op 4 TBL_OP_QUERY_CLEAR_CT    -> _tbl_clear_ct
  //     op 5 TBL_OP_QUERY_PRESENT_CT  -> _tbl_present_ct
  //     else                             INVOKE_UNSUPPORTED
  //
  // Rights gate: every op requires R_TBL_READ (0x001). target_ptr
  // is ignored at skeleton stage; a future per-table layout would
  // use it as a table cap selector (today there is one global
  // table).
  //
  // SysV: rdi = rights, rsi = target_ptr, rdx = op_arg.
  // Stack recipe: 3 callee-save pushes (rbx = rights, r12 = target_
  //   ptr, r13 = op_code).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let R_TBL_READ : u64 = 0x001

  pub let TBL_OP_QUERY_INITED      : u64 = 0
  pub let TBL_OP_QUERY_INIT_CT     : u64 = 1
  pub let TBL_OP_QUERY_SCOL_CT     : u64 = 2
  pub let TBL_OP_QUERY_APPEND_CT   : u64 = 3
  pub let TBL_OP_QUERY_CLEAR_CT    : u64 = 4
  pub let TBL_OP_QUERY_PRESENT_CT  : u64 = 5

  pub let cap_handler_table : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{cap} =
    fn (rights: u64, target_ptr: u64, op_arg: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {cap},
      justification: "Wave 83 G17 (paideia-os#2554) skeleton: KIND_TABLE_PANE (0x59) cap_invoke dispatch. Entry chatter (klog_s1 of tbl_tag_handler_entry). op_code = op_arg & 0xFF; rights gate against R_TBL_READ (single up-front check); dispatch 0..5 to the matching getter (table_inited / table_init_ct / table_scol_ct / table_append_ct / table_clear_ct / table_present_ct); else INVOKE_UNSUPPORTED. target_ptr is masked to its low byte on entry as a defensive bound for a future per-table layout widen (today there is one global table). Three callee-save pushes land rsp%16==0 at every nested call. The mutating ops (init / set_column / append / clear / present) are deferred to a follow-up slice that either extends cap_invoke with a 4-register slot variant or packs the args into target_ptr/op_arg. Labels prefixed tbl_hd_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;

        mov rbx, rdi;                       // rights
        mov r12, rsi;
        mov r10, 0xFF;
        and r12, r10;                       // target = target_ptr[7:0]
        mov r13, rdx;                       // op_arg
        and r13, r10;                       // op_code = op_arg[7:0]

        // Entry chatter.
        mov rdi, 3;                         // LEVEL_INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_DRV_];
        lea rdx, [rip + tbl_tag_handler_entry];
        call klog_s1;

        // Rights gate.
        mov r10, rbx;
        and r10, 0x001;                     // R_TBL_READ
        cmp r10, 0;
        je  tbl_hd_denied;

        // Op dispatch.
        cmp r13, 0;
        je  tbl_hd_op_inited;
        cmp r13, 1;
        je  tbl_hd_op_init_ct;
        cmp r13, 2;
        je  tbl_hd_op_scol_ct;
        cmp r13, 3;
        je  tbl_hd_op_app_ct;
        cmp r13, 4;
        je  tbl_hd_op_clr_ct;
        cmp r13, 5;
        je  tbl_hd_op_pres_ct;
        jmp tbl_hd_unsup;

      tbl_hd_op_inited:
        call table_inited;
        jmp tbl_hd_out;

      tbl_hd_op_init_ct:
        call table_init_ct;
        jmp tbl_hd_out;

      tbl_hd_op_scol_ct:
        call table_scol_ct;
        jmp tbl_hd_out;

      tbl_hd_op_app_ct:
        call table_append_ct;
        jmp tbl_hd_out;

      tbl_hd_op_clr_ct:
        call table_clear_ct;
        jmp tbl_hd_out;

      tbl_hd_op_pres_ct:
        call table_present_ct;
        jmp tbl_hd_out;

      tbl_hd_denied:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFD;        // INVOKE_DENIED
        jmp tbl_hd_out;
      tbl_hd_unsup:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC;        // INVOKE_UNSUPPORTED

      tbl_hd_out:
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §O  Boot wiring note
  // ----------------
  // kernel_main.pdx does NOT need a dedicated reset entry: .bss
  // zero-init leaves _tbl_state empty (bo_cap=0, max_cols=0, max_
  // rows=0, cur_rows=0, inited=0 -- so set_column / append / clear
  // / present all refuse until init is called), _col_meta zeroed
  // (every column reports width=0, align=0=left before set_column),
  // _cell_table zeroed (every cell reports utf8_ptr=0, utf8_len=0),
  // and the five counters at zero. A follow-up slice may mint a
  // defensive `table_reset` for parity with the other dpy drivers'
  // reset entries, but the skeleton gets by on .bss alone.
  //
  // invoke.pdx picks up the KIND_TABLE_PANE (0x59) dispatch arm in
  // the same slice as this file -- the arm is pure plumbing and
  // self-standing (handler returns INVOKE_UNSUPPORTED for every
  // mutating op at skeleton stage, which is observable but harmless).
  //
  // No new klog wrapper is minted; the four fingerprints ride
  // klog_s1_d2 (INIT, SET_COL, APPEND) and klog_s1 (CLEAR), all
  // pre-existing in klog/wrappers.pdx.
  //
  // Follow-up slices (G18 and later):
  //   - Cell-copy body in table_append_row (deref cells_ptr as array
  //     of (utf8_ptr, utf8_len) pairs; store into _cell_table at
  //     cur_rows; bump cur_rows).
  //   - SDF glyph quad stamper in table_present (per-cell SDF
  //     lookup + justification against _col_meta[c].width_chars /
  //     .align; stamp into GPU BO).
  //   - direct_scanout_arm plumbing in table_present (behind an
  //     eligibility gate on bo_cap for pipe 0).
  //   - Dirty-row bitmap + damage_plane_submit integration (only
  //     re-stamp the rows that changed since the last present).
  //   - TBL_MAX_ROWS widen from 256 to 1024 once a kernel-link bss
  //     capacity check has run (the task directive's primary target
  //     was 1024; the skeleton lands with 256 per the directive's
  //     explicit `Default to 256 rows if 1024 doesn't fit` escape
  //     clause).
  //   - cap_handler extension for the mutating ops once cap_invoke
  //     gains a 4-register slot variant OR the shell is willing to
  //     pack (bo_cap, cols, rows) into target_ptr/op_arg for init.
  //   - gpu_bo_alloc multi-page carve so a full 16*1024 table fits
  //     in a single BO (today's Wave 75 BO backs <= 128 cells).
  // ==========================================================================
}
